  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_8848705937094fb892d457edf884aa09",
      "statement": "The `manifold-eval` console entry infers the evaluation policy from the before artifact's own `model_index.json` `pipeline_class` rather than a mode flag: `LatentFlowPipeline` routes to the unconditional same-noise pass and `ControlNetLatentFlowPipeline` routes to the paired pass against real targets; an unknown class or a directory without `model_index.json` fails fast.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/cli.py#L132-L165",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2dff360e6a172ed549e51f000b8f245d179bcd3d36ec24864623bfe719ecde6a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/cli.py#L260-L331",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:26c3eed7c23d3c689cccf39617d92cc836bc09c09520e5daf84703a778ab0d91:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6939b87b2fbf425895da11033b6b6558",
      "statement": "The before/after driver owns the fairness invariant: the unconditional path hands each side a fresh generator seeded identically, and the paired path draws one noise tensor and passes the same tensor to both sides, so any output difference is attributable to the policy weights rather than sampling stochasticity.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/before_after.py#L104-L159",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:668340afde6cfd2a64df40699c821793b933680dcf2290ee94dd6af421f647f4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/before_after.py#L163-L199",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bd2fdd2ef509fb77c42a9ae99e1633cba7a82c710ec2a273ffd5704f319eb26e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d8d9ee8af087488798afb174c82316c4",
      "statement": "`manifold-eval` exports the after checkpoint through the existing checkpoint-to-native bridge into `<output>/after_native` and then reloads both native exports into fresh pipelines, because the bridge bakes the after weights into the probe pipeline's components in place.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/before_after.py#L1-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f0da07aa7f2bc385b1cb00c47fc88b017340e512e7ba6901307d04454dff7d17:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/cli.py#L262-L286",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ad6ed76608a580cfa104e2c6a2086170054d888f3dc16a60c093dcbf430f023f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_081fab602f604ff68b8e920834372b67",
      "statement": "Every evaluated volume — before, after, and the real target — is decoded through the same float32 `LatentDecoder` path and per-sample `min_max_to_unit` normalization to [0,1], which is what lets the paired metric assume `data_range = 1.0` and makes the offline numbers comparable with the in-training monitor.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/before_after.py#L82-L94",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:321a8fdec1fc36142709a26b0755561321573b61e005bbc81a77b60d56696667:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/pipelines/pipeline_utils.py#L26-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dd122d6dc1889d50fab432e7bf7aaee3d34496e86896526cef80d6f922291a9e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b49ad2fb9aa247638a06215e8b02a87f",
      "statement": "The offline artifact contract is a `metrics.json` recording policy, seed, inference-step count, sample count and grid basenames, plus per-side `before`/`after` PSNR and SSIM for the paired policy only; the JiT record intentionally carries no fidelity scalars, and grid references are basenames so the directory stays portable.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/before_after.py#L147-L156",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:74d37cac36a28716d4ca89e744e3e54aee9fb800351e417c781c4ac8ec1cdd2c:"
        },
        {
